    "render": 3,
    "verbatimUserPrompt": "${verbatimUserPrompt}",
    "userIntent": "${userIntent}"
  }
]
```

These show only two input fields for illustration; the complete templates include all state fields.

The workflow supplies the captured values. Most transitions simply fill the specified fields, preserve previously captured values, and advance the render. Only the branching transitions inspect a value—such as ${exampleMatch}, ${mode}, or whether ${requirements} is empty—to determine the destination state.

Created **24 non-branching transitions plus initialization** in [transitions.json](https://github.com/BestNameYet/StateMachines/blob/main/ChatMachines/Workflow%20Interactive%20Procedures/AGENTS%20Procedure/transitions.json).

Each specifies only updated fields, then calls the renderer:

